{"patched_source": "from django.contrib.auth.mixins import LoginRequiredMixin
from django.views import generic
from .models import Post


class PostList(LoginRequiredMixin, generic.ListView):
    queryset = Post.objects.filter(status=1).order_by('-created_on')
    template_name = 'index.html'

class PostDetail(generic.DetailView):
    model = Post
    template_name = 'post_detail.html'
", "explanation": "The /eee/ page is served by PostList, which previously inherited only generic.ListView and therefore returned HTTP 200 to unauthenticated visitors, allowing the vertical privilege escalation. The fix adds Django's built-in LoginRequiredMixin as the first base class on PostList and includes it via the existing Django auth mixins module (django.contrib.auth.mixins), which is the project-appropriate guard context since no custom auth sentinel, role, owner variable, or denial marker exists in the validated snippets. This reuses Django's standard denial semantics: anonymous users are redirected to LOGIN_URL before the queryset is evaluated or any protected content is returned, while authenticated authorized roles (user1, user2) continue to access the list, satisfying both the exploit-block and regression-pass requirements. No other logic, queryset, template, or view was modified, and no role/owner check was added that would over-restrict authorized users."}
